[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2840571508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2840571508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2840571508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pT650","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T01:13:17Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T01:13:17Z","body":"Some thoughts regarding the documentation / scripting API:\r\n\r\n- `reserve` and `reverse` visually look very similar and could easily be swapped. Maybe a more explicit name like `reserve_capacity` or similar could be found?\r\n- Docs don't really clarify the difference between `reserve` and `resize`. To me, they seem really similar, so I wouldn't know when to use which one... They should maybe also link to each other, since they seem related.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2840571508/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841412084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2841412084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2841412084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pXIH0","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T09:43:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T09:43:57Z","body":"Doing god's work.\r\n\r\n> * `reserve` and `reverse` visually look very similar and could easily be swapped. Maybe a more explicit name like `reserve_capacity` or similar could be found?\r\n\r\nI do agree, but to play devil's advocate, one has a required parameter and the other does not even have any. Still, is it a good idea to expose it? Could it be done separately?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841412084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841475109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2841475109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2841475109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pXXgl","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T10:07:22Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T10:07:40Z","body":"> I do agree, but to play devil's advocate, one has a required parameter and the other does not even have any. Still, is it a good idea to expose it? Could it be done separately?\r\n\r\nI'm open to the idea of not exposing it (for now?).\r\nGDScript has a lot of overhead, so `reserve` has a lot less of a measurable effect there as opposed to core. Or at least that's what I suspect. I've been meaning to test this.\r\n\r\nAs to the names, even in core we have the same problem. `LocalVector` also has both `reverse` and `reserve` already. If we want to choose a different name, we'll have rename all uses of reserve!\r\n(And if we go _there_, we actually may want to change it to `reserve_more` semantics since that just makes a lot more sense 😅)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841475109/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841496393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2841496393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2841496393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pXctJ","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T10:16:13Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T10:16:13Z","body":"> GDScript has a lot of overhead, so `reserve` has a lot less of a measurable effect there as opposed to core. Or at least that's what I suspect. I've been meaning to test this.\r\n\r\nEven then, the expectation for Array in GDScript is that... it just works, more so than doing so efficiently. On the other hand, Packed arrays are generally expected to be fast (by extension of being compact) so the inclusion of this method sounds more justified there. Still, worth testing.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2841496393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845830646","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2845830646","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2845830646,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pn-32","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T21:33:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T23:42:39Z","body":"I've run an extensive suite of performance tests to make sure there are only marginal regressions at worst, but improvements otherwise. It led me to some re-writes, which also happened to make the code less complex (in my opinion). I'm very happy with it overall now.\r\n\r\nMost notably, `push_back` can be 2x faster than before as-is, and using `reserve` alongside it can be up to 6x faster (in total).\r\n\r\nI also tested that it makes sense from GDScript, where I can see an up to 20% measurable improvement when using `reserve` (in the best case). As expected, it's not _that_ interesting (as opposed to in `Core`), but it's at least _somewhat_ interesting.\r\n\r\nEdit: Sorry about repeated pushes, GCC is raising a lot of false-positive warnings...\r\nEdit2: I think the final error on Mono isn't _totally_ related? It sounds like the C# bindings are incorrectly using a `String` of sorts which ends up pushing an error, triggering the same problem again... :/","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845830646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847858209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2847858209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2847858209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pvt4h","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T18:38:06Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T10:41:11Z","body":"C# had a problem in that the new `capacity` made the placement of `size` with regards to `_ptr` indeterministic (across platforms): While in arm / x86, the max alignment is 8 bytes and thus the relative offset is unchanged - but in x64, the max alignment is 16 bytes, which means `DATA_OFFSET` is aligned by an additional 8 bytes.\r\nSince C# is not capable of querying alignment (and it's also somewhat compiler dependent), I needed to change its implementation to defer to C++ instead. This change would be expected sooner or later anyway, at least if C# is to be moved to GDExtension.\r\n\r\nEdit: Sorry for repeated pushes; I tried to get away without installing C# tooling locally, which apparently was a bad idea 😅","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847858209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943662343","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928#issuecomment-2943662343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105928","id":2943662343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vdLkH","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}",